# StudentStack — Cursor Rules (strict)

## Brand & UI/UX
- Visual language: extreme modern roundness (large border radii), bubbly rounded sans-serif typography, soft and vibrant pastels, thick drop shadows, playful bouncy hover animations (reference: Duolingo, Kalshi energy).
- Interactions: prefer `motion` / CSS transitions with subtle scale and shadow on hover; avoid flat static panels without feedback.

## Icons
- Never use generic placeholder icons, emoji-as-icons for UI chrome, or “AI JSON” / stock robot icons.
- Use **Lucide React** (or other curated SVG icon libraries) or intentional **CSS shapes** only.

## Product & Content Boundaries
- **StudentStack** public surface is **newsletter + certifications**.
- Landing hero: student-led daily for parents (do not over-explain; social traffic already knows the pitch). Avoid repeating “free” in hero body when the CTA already says it.
- **Certifications** are the clear paid student pathway on the public site (priced, timeline-driven).
- **StudentStack Elite** (parent/student portal) may be soft-upsold from the daily later; do not hard-sell checkout or “24/7 concierge” on the landing page until productized.
- Do **not** advertise course catalogs on the landing page.
- The “college student team” presentation is a branding layer.

## Engineering defaults
- App is Next.js at the repo root. Prefer extending the operator newsletter pipeline (`/operator`, `/api/admin/*`, `/api/cron/*`) over new frameworks.
